  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently, SetOwner takes effect after a delay. If you have a simple on/off switch this means you need a bunch of extra logic to deal with maintaining local state while you attempt to gain ownership, as otherwise any local changes to synced variables will be overwritten. Having a variant of SetOwner that effectively stops incoming syncing for the object until the ownership change attempt completes (successfully or otherwise) would make a lot of simple use cases much easier.",
